Package: RAILS
Title: Raking with Assisted Nested Propensity Score and LIFO Selection
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Huiding", "Chen", email = "extrasane@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5102-434X"))
Description: Combines a non-probability sample (e.g. a volunteer biobank) with
    a probability reference sample to produce population-representative
    weights. The core estimator fits a pseudo-likelihood propensity model on
    all interactions up to a base order, selects higher-order interactions by
    a forward likelihood-ratio test, and applies last-in-first-out stepwise
    raking to reference population margins. All computation runs on aggregated
    covariate cells. Variance is available from a stacked estimating-equation
    sandwich that accounts for uncertainty in the estimated weights, and a
    subgroup wrapper runs the procedure within levels of a stratifying
    variable.
